WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.804
Now we start combining several ideas into a more
realistic rule We

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:10.366
want active patients who explicitly consented to
contact have either Diabetes or

00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:15.007
Kidney Disease and do not have a usable email
address Notice how

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:20.806
carefully the requirements are defined Active must
be true Consent

00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:27.030
must explicitly be true UNKNOWN consent is not
treated as permission The

00:00:27.056 --> 00:00:32.924
diagnosis must be one of the target diagnoses
Finally we normalize

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.938
the email before checking whether it is missing The
full query is

00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:41.960
available in the code cell Run it in the browser and
examine

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:46.904
each returned record against the written rule You
can also copy the

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:51.674
query into pgAdmin This is a good example of
translating a real

00:00:51.686 --> 00:00:55.179
requirement into several small testable SQL
conditions
